          <h2 id="unexpected-results">Unexpected results</h2>

          <details id="abort-early" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6" open>
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words"
                >Only one issue comes back, but several fields are wrong</span
              >
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                <strong>Cause.</strong> <code>abortEarly</code> and{' '}
                <code>abortEarlyOnEachField</code> both default to <strong>true</strong>. Pass{' '}
                <code>&#123; abortEarly: false &#125;</code> to collect every field's issues.
              </p>
              <CodeBlock code={abortEarlyExample} language="typescript" />
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                Inside an array element every field runs to completion whatever you passed, so
                one bad element never hides its siblings.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details id="missing-field-passes" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6">
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words">A missing field passes validation</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                <strong>Cause.</strong> There is no implicit <code>required</code>: a field
                that declares no presence rule accepts a missing value —{' '}
                <a href="/docs/core-concepts#presence">presence</a>. Add{' '}
                <code>.required()</code>.
              </p>
              <CodeBlock code={implicitRequiredExample} language="typescript" />
            </div>
          </details>

          <details id="transform-did-not-run" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6">
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words">A transform did not run</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                <strong>Cause.</strong> Transforms run only in <code>parse()</code>, and
                always last, whatever the chain order —{' '}
                <a href="/docs/core-concepts#the-order-rules-run-in">the one order</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details id="gate-order" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6">
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words"
                >A gate ran too late, or a conditional produced the wrong issue</span
              >
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <ul class="md-body-medium space-y-2 text-on-surface-variant">
                <li>
                  <strong><code>validateIf</code> / <code>skip</code>.</strong> Every gate on
                  a field is asked before any check runs —{' '}
                  <a href="/docs/core-concepts#the-order-rules-run-in">rule order</a>.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <strong><code>requiredIf</code> / <code>optionalIf</code>.</strong> Presence
                  rules, not checks: one issue, and the rest of the chain does not run —{' '}
                  <a href="/docs/core-concepts#presence">presence</a>.
                </li>
              </ul>
              <CodeBlock code={gateOrderExample} language="typescript" />
            </div>
          </details>

          <details id="strict-extra-property" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6">
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words"
                ><code>strict()</code> did not reject an extra property</span
              >
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                <strong>Cause.</strong> <code>strict()</code> is a compile-time obligation
                that every leaf path of your type is declared. It has no runtime effect at
                all. Rejecting unknown properties is a rule: use{' '}
                <code>objectAdditionalProperties</code>, documented on the{' '}
                <a href="/docs/api/builder#extra-properties">Builder page</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <h2 id="messages">Messages and codes</h2>

          <details id="error-codes" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6" open>
