                A call-level <code>messageFactory</code> and <code>translate</code> option
                existed in 1.x's <code>ValidationOptions</code>. Both are gone; pass the
                factory per rule.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <h2 id="async">Async checks</h2>

          <details id="async-lookup" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6" open>
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words"
                >Checking a value against a database or an API</span
              >
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                The whole <code>@maroonedog/luq/async</code> subpath is one{' '}
                <code>await</code> followed by the ordinary synchronous engine. It contains no
                rule, no plan and no loop over fields.
              </p>
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                The <code>external</code> validate option is the pre-resolved bag that{' '}
                <code>@maroonedog/luq/plugins/fromContext</code> reads;{' '}
                <code>@maroonedog/luq/async</code> resolves the promises and passes them in on
                it.
              </p>
              <CodeBlock code={asyncExample} language="typescript" fileName="signup.ts" />

              <div class="rounded-shape-md bg-surface-container p-4">
                <p class="md-label-large mb-2">Three names, and what each one is</p>
                <ul class="md-body-medium space-y-2 text-on-surface-variant">
                  <li>
                    <code>createAsyncContext()</code> — an immutable builder;{' '}
                    <code>.set(key, promise)</code> returns a new one, and{' '}
                    <code>.build()</code> resolves everything with{' '}
                    <code>Promise.allSettled</code>, so entries run in parallel.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <code>addAsyncSupport(validator)</code> — adds{' '}
                    <code>withAsyncContext</code> without putting a fifth method on the core
                    validator.
                  </li>
                  <li>
                    <code>readAsyncContext(ruleContext, isContext)</code> — the read side, for
                    plugin authors. It takes the guard that <em>proves</em> the shape, so a
                    context that never resolved cannot masquerade as one that did. 1.x called
                    it <code>getAsyncContext(context)</code> and asserted instead.
                  </li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details id="async-failure" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6">
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
