              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                With <code>continueOnError</code> left off, a failed entry makes{' '}
                <code>isReady</code> false and the bound validator rejects immediately with
                one issue per failure, path = the entry's key and code{' '}
                <code>asyncContextUnavailable</code>. No field rule runs.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <h2 id="bundle-size">Bundle size</h2>

          <details id="bundle-larger" class="not-prose md-card md-card-outlined mb-6 p-6" open>
            <summary class="md-title-medium flex cursor-pointer items-center gap-2">
              <span class="summary-marker md-icon md-icon-sm" aria-hidden="true"
                >expand_more</span
              >
              <span class="min-w-0 break-words">More Luq in the bundle than expected</span>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                First, check what "expected" was. Every entry is measured and re-measured by
                CI on every build:{' '}
                <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2" href="/benchmarks#bundle-size"
                  >the bundle size table</a
                >. The floor is {bundleSize.coreOnly.gzip} for{' '}
                <code>Builder</code> with no plugins.
              </p>
              <p class="md-body-medium text-on-surface-variant">
                Adding a plugin costs 129–224 B of gzip, so if your bundle is much larger than
                the core plus your plugin count, something is pulling in more than you named.
              </p>
              <CodeBlock code={importCostExample} language="typescript" />
              <ul class="md-body-medium space-y-2 text-on-surface-variant">
                <li>
                  The barrel is <strong>not</strong> the problem when your bundler
                  tree-shakes — it was measured at a 1 B difference over three plugins, which
                  gzip to {bundleSize.threePlugin.gzip} through the subpaths, and{' '}
                  <code>check:barrel-equivalence</code> fails the build if the two routes
                  diverge by more than {barrelDivergencePercent}%. Check that you are emitting
                  ES modules and that tree-shaking is on.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <code>jsonSchemaFullFeature</code> bundles the plugins a whole document
                  needs, which is why one import covers it. The <code>jsonSchema</code> route
                  is billed as the tree-shakeable half and measured it is not — use it for the
                  chain method, not to save bytes. Both are in{' '}
                  <a class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2" href="/benchmarks#bundle-size"
                    >the bundle size table</a
                  >.
                </li>
                <li>
                  <code>import * as plugins from '…'</code> defeats tree-shaking in most
                  bundlers. Name what you import.
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </details>

          <h2 id="performance">Performance</h2>

